GET_RAW_DATA – Build Request Header (gs_header) and WBS Items (gt_wbs_items) from PROJ/PRPS/BPGE/V_IVP_PR/IMPR
Objective
Build:

Header structure gs_header (type ZTB_A2R_WBSHDR-like) from PROJ, plus PR master data from V_IVP_PR, plus investment reason from IMPR.
Item internal table gt_wbs_items (type ZTB_A2R_WBSITEM) from PRPS, enriched with cost values from BPGE and PR attributes from V_IVP_PR.

Input

iv_pspid_proj (type ZTB_A2R_WBSHDR-PSPID) — Project Definition external ID (PROJ-PSPID).

Output

gs_header populated (project header + PR header + investment reason + optional unifier).
gt_wbs_items populated (WBS lines).


A) Source Reads (What to SELECT)
A1) PROJ (Project Header)
Selection:

Read exactly one row from PROJ where PROJ-PSPID = iv_pspid_proj.
Fields required:
PSPNR, POST1, ERNAM, ERDAT, VERNR, VBUKR, VKOKR, PRCTR, PLSEZ, WERKS, PROFL, KOSTL

Derived:

Use PROJ-PSPNR as internal project number for PRPS selection.


A2) PRPS (WBS Items)
Selection:

Read all PRPS where PRPS-PSPHI = PROJ-PSPNR (internal number from PROJ).
Fields required:
POSID, POST1, OBJNR, PBUKR, PKOKR, WERKS, STUFE, PKSTL, ZUNIFIER_PROJ
(and any additional PRPS fields required by your structure)


A3) BPGE (Costs / Budget-like Values)
For each PRPS-OBJNR, get:
A3.1 KSTP → WTGES (highest ledger)

Filter: BPGE-OBJNR = PRPS-OBJNR AND BPGE-VORGA = 'KSTP'
Rule: pick records where ledger is the highest for that OBJNR (e.g., MAX(LEDNR)).
Value: aggregate WTGES at that highest ledger (use SUM(WTGES) to avoid multi-line ambiguity).

Result mapping: gt_wbs_items-wert2 = SUM(BPGE-wtges) at highest ledger for KSTP
A3.2 KBUD → GEBER (highest ledger, non-initial)

Filter: BPGE-OBJNR = PRPS-OBJNR AND BPGE-VORGA = 'KBUD' AND BPGE-GEBER is not initial
Rule: pick highest ledger for that OBJNR (e.g., MAX(LEDNR) with those filters).
Value: take a deterministic value if multiple lines exist (e.g., MAX(GEBER)).

Result: keep in a lookup map keyed by OBJNR (assign to a target field only if you have one; otherwise keep for later use).

A4) V_IVP_PR (PR Attributes per POSID)
For each PRPS-POSID, select:

V_IVP_PR-PRNAM, GJAHR, POSNR, PRART
Filter:
V_IVP_PR-POSID = PRPS-POSID

Important rule (per your request):

No need to compute max GJAHR.
If multiple rows exist for same POSID, the logic “just gets it” — meaning it picks the first match you decide (common approach: sort by POSID then take first row per POSID, or simply read first found).

Result mapping:

gs_header-prnam, gs_header-gjahr, gs_header-posnr filled using the first available V_IVP_PR row encountered (only fill if header fields are initial to avoid overwriting).
gt_wbs_items-gjahr, gt_wbs_items-prart filled per item POSID.


A5) IMPR (Investment Program Reason)
Using V_IVP_PR-POSNR:

Select IMPR-IZWEK
Filter:
IMPR-POSNR = V_IVP_PR-POSNR

Result mapping:

gs_header-izwek = IMPR-izwek (fill once, only if header field is initial).


B) Detailed Field Mapping
B1) Header Mapping: PROJ → GS_HEADER

gs_header-mandt ← sy-mandt
gs_header-pspnr ← proj-pspnr
gs_header-post1 ← proj-post1
gs_header-ernam ← proj-ernam
gs_header-erdat ← proj-erdat
gs_header-vernr ← proj-vernr
gs_header-bukrs ← proj-vbukr
gs_header-vkokr ← proj-vkokr
gs_header-prctr ← proj-prctr
gs_header-plsez ← proj-plsez
gs_header-werks ← proj-werks
gs_header-profl ← proj-profl
gs_header-kostl ← proj-kostl

B2) Header Mapping: PRPS/V_IVP_PR/IMPR → GS_HEADER

gs_header-zunifier_proj ← first non-initial prps-zunifier_proj encountered
gs_header-prnam ← first available v_ivp_pr-prnam (only if initial)
gs_header-gjahr ← first available v_ivp_pr-gjahr (only if initial)
gs_header-posnr ← first available v_ivp_pr-posnr (only if initial)
gs_header-izwek ← impr-izwek where impr-posnr = gs_header-posnr (only if initial)


B3) Item Mapping: PRPS → GT_WBS_ITEMS
For each PRPS row:

gt_wbs_items-mandt ← sy-mandt
gt_wbs_items-pspid ← iv_pspid_proj
gt_wbs_items-posid ← prps-posid
gt_wbs_items-post1 ← prps-post1
gt_wbs_items-bukrs ← prps-pbukr
gt_wbs_items-vkokr ← prps-pkokr
gt_wbs_items-stufe ← prps-stufe
gt_wbs_items-werks ← prps-werks

B4) Item Enrichment: BPGE → GT_WBS_ITEMS
Per item (via prps-objnr):

gt_wbs_items-wert2 ← SUM(bpge-wtges) where:

bpge-objnr = prps-objnr
bpge-vorga = 'KSTP'
ledger = highest (e.g., max lednr) for that objnr



(Optionally keep KBUD→GEBER in memory keyed by OBJNR if you need it later.)
B5) Item Enrichment: V_IVP_PR → GT_WBS_ITEMS
Per item (via prps-posid):

gt_wbs_items-gjahr ← v_ivp_pr-gjahr
gt_wbs_items-prart ← v_ivp_pr-prart


C) Processing Order (Algorithm)

Read PROJ header by PSPID.
Read PRPS items by PSPHI = PROJ-PSPNR.
Build unique lists:

OBJNR list from PRPS for BPGE queries
POSID list from PRPS for V_IVP_PR queries


Read BPGE aggregation:

max ledger per OBJNR for KSTP → then sum WTGES at that ledger
max ledger per OBJNR for KBUD with geber not initial → then pick geber


Read V_IVP_PR by POSID (no max gjahr logic).
Read IMPR by POSNR from V_IVP_PR to get IZWEK.
Loop PRPS:

build item row from PRPS fields
assign wert2 from BPGE KSTP map
assign gjahr/prart from V_IVP_PR map
fill header PRNAM/GJAHR/POSNR/IZWEK only once (if initial)
append item to gt_wbs_items
